#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23935fc7-68d8-5aac-8f46-503e8ec88a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+3z+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336366} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba1cad0-4734-5fa1-b087-ec9799500799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+y-2z+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336593} {:answer/id #uuid "93b0ebf0-a8e8-5f44-8eb9-023cde940780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+3z+5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337381} {:answer/id #uuid "95222014-68cb-59f3-a573-b24be1101543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+3z+8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337393} {:answer/id #uuid "980f75c8-ef08-5f4b-af72-5fc63238fa4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y+2z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337419}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336366} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5064e0e-2c84-5880-be2a-969020b41c72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c143f82e-4ed3-5f75-863a-8c48f0e6d896" :question/math-academy-id "q-70805" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-1,1,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=i+j+3k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-1,1,-2⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨1,1,3⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ & =⟨-1,1,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,3⟩ & =-6 \\\\ x+y+3z & =-6 \\\\ x+y+3z+6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e82b227-9a56-5114-8d60-f1db519ee0d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+y+z-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336168} {:answer/id #uuid "8f404ec9-8911-54fa-8613-a6198b2c338f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3y-z-14=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337324} {:answer/id #uuid "a94ce30c-4842-5698-bc28-64b32c7460e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2y-2z-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337560} {:answer/id #uuid "b98b2fc3-d714-56e3-8598-185596415529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-z-14=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337676} {:answer/id #uuid "bad68854-37a9-54dc-a14b-ae58354b47a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2y-2z-14=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337689}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337689} :answer-field/id #uuid "23126fc2-1b82-57e0-8166-f43f5a36d945" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "743ee1e7-8110-5025-8c98-4fb7a2685168" :question/math-academy-id "q-70809" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$$\n\\displaystyle r=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨3,2,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨3,2,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ & =⟨2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-2⟩ & =14 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z & =14 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z-14 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b4cf333-fb31-53e5-a3b2-4d1da8c129ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337143} {:answer/id #uuid "8699f13d-227d-54e9-8db2-f586a65cc4a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337250} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed87010-5adf-5b37-aeca-2e7df330c813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337317} {:answer/id #uuid "92eae00f-5f08-53b6-b534-72b9e6866cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337371} {:answer/id #uuid "a20a8aa3-4bd5-5bea-8e7e-61c74a32567a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337501}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337317} :answer-field/id #uuid "557fd6f3-4749-5c34-935d-a0b820019a0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22393ec9-8250-54f3-ad30-3ecff187a9da" :question/math-academy-id "q-70814" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,1⟩=10.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,1⟩=10$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-2,1⟩ & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1}-2{t}_{2}+{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =2{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{2} \\\\ 2{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021e4e67-7010-5485-9b89-cfeeb7d10451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336050} {:answer/id #uuid "05f44b25-e549-5024-872e-4c4912f94181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336080} {:answer/id #uuid "39aee5e7-07d0-54c2-87e3-baadc590c41e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336574} {:answer/id #uuid "68913fec-0010-53ce-97fd-f1effeb01d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336964} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ebba20-fcb1-5c49-9ea4-d8297f4c6a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338173}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336574} :answer-field/id #uuid "c81f1744-1b47-5344-b32f-ae5d1db03724" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7945519-2cef-57b7-a592-36730597689e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70817" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,0,1⟩=5.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨3,0,1⟩=5$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,0,1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,0,1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}+{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =-3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},-3{t}_{1}⟩\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46a8c73e-1b6f-5ead-8b4e-04fd47ae71ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336688} {:answer/id #uuid "566ad7e4-2332-5818-b1ab-63f151123755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336827} {:answer/id #uuid "6955aab1-e2a7-5bda-a291-b54a99b1d9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336968} {:answer/id #uuid "806b2ca4-42eb-53b0-90bb-44522d3b01e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337195} {:answer/id #uuid "d93906ff-8ee7-57c5-a797-f2d48eaf72f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337922}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336688} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac53d05e-4ae9-5aad-8699-2cdc5ab0d589" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c12dba6-0a5e-5abe-ba85-6c6b625059ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-70822" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-5,-1,4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,-5,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4dafb7-c1e3-52bb-9be6-8c920a5e0c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336620} {:answer/id #uuid "8adc6dd8-06c3-54d2-9922-36b4707070b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337284} {:answer/id #uuid "9a72c942-01f6-5ae4-80c1-9074296dcd5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337434} {:answer/id #uuid "bac2e877-851a-58b5-bda5-b1f53f68e73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337687} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b3af4d-d5d3-54b2-80fd-fb6b4c38bce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338180}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337284} :answer-field/id #uuid "f28575a2-8621-51a3-b18b-ae5aadfa4d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31208d04-81a2-5a09-afcd-1cbba801d10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70828" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,2,-4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -2{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3} \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ad3af79-fcd3-5749-b0e5-9411379a50d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336721} {:answer/id #uuid "886c099c-bd36-506a-9021-b550fe0b57c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337264} {:answer/id #uuid "926d8af8-a19c-5443-bbf7-6f269886e17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337364} {:answer/id #uuid "d60f66f3-48fa-5ebf-837a-e090ca7d3d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337896} {:answer/id #uuid "d99cfee8-de55-5ea6-8c2e-3385468433bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337925}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337896} :answer-field/id #uuid "7727c896-6f1b-5615-b00c-42ad7fd27f9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0327785-b28b-5842-b652-0805899123b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-70830" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,-3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10191765-520e-51b1-b616-6aed299a1951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336181} {:answer/id #uuid "7daf1c63-6468-51ad-b441-f7fb571f725e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3z+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337169} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9bfc06-e53d-546a-8e5c-41d1b1999a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337685} {:answer/id #uuid "c52efad2-ab20-5349-b4af-05ecdf7d704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337785} {:answer/id #uuid "f09bbdc2-0929-5b68-b7a0-f2e4bd00ad0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3y-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338137}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338137} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f92cb71-8832-51de-ba25-618de4d73dc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee138f11-2a9e-5208-a49a-f5a947f6c08b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70833" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,0,-3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,2,0⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨2,0,-3⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2i+3j \\\\  & =⟨2,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =⟨2,0,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =4 \\\\ 2x+3y & =4 \\\\ 2x+3y-4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62f42755-b7a1-5809-87fc-9e17362d71bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=⟨4,-2,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336923} {:answer/id #uuid "682d20d3-364d-50e6-9603-4089e146e80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336962} {:answer/id #uuid "79bd5faa-c481-5160-a5a8-d577ea7ae9c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337127} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c6d7e8-9c47-5c5e-ac67-b2edb2098ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,3⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337667} {:answer/id #uuid "bad32934-1f86-5ba6-bb6a-9563a6f86fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,3⟩=⟨2,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336962} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ebd3bcf-abcc-5e66-8e50-5b3cd1690259" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac6804de-8b54-5910-a3f3-3c7b3ad0197c" :question/math-academy-id "q-70893" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(4,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-1,0,1)$ and $B(1,0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨4,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-1,0,1)$ and $B(1,0,-1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,0,-1⟩-⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨2,0,-2⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e51591-bf02-5474-aec8-30aa3e188bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336071} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd38a34-b3ab-59ce-b0e6-a6d3b8de493e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336292} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb00c21-c6bb-5559-9485-37476b9643af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336442} {:answer/id #uuid "70fbd409-4407-5d02-94e5-220dccec345b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=⟨2,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337038} {:answer/id #uuid "ab1a3637-079a-538d-96f7-2cf741de3741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337576}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336292} :answer-field/id #uuid "02ec79e2-ec6f-57fd-ace8-21faef1197d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d76bf424-d04c-5aa9-b260-23e0fb3325ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-70894" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+t \\\\ y &=2-t \\\\ z &=3+2t.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+t \\\\ y &=2-t \\\\ z &=3+2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩+t\\text{ }\\underbrace{⟨1,-1,2⟩}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =⟨2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00227479-5977-5397-9100-1b17106f6f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336032} {:answer/id #uuid "7a23ffb5-90fe-5574-8788-b35cd3472639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337130} {:answer/id #uuid "8bc69e15-be00-5985-8928-5ae6da0b85fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-4,1⟩+s⟨-1,0,4⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337298} {:answer/id #uuid "9df3fd4f-c200-56e8-801d-837062abe73d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,0,4⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337460} {:answer/id #uuid "f73323f6-d68a-5f33-a1ce-fe11e5050b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338199}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337460} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d334158-7c9e-5eb8-85d7-5810eda2f8fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2b043ce-2959-5d1e-9542-cf409b778a9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70965" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-1,0,4)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $Q$ is $p=⟨-1,0,4⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1,0,4⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42395827-35cc-56c8-be64-dcb4273beb95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336657} {:answer/id #uuid "5349233e-7692-537c-ab4f-6921abbd6820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336799} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b1e1d5-44e4-596d-90f9-5b7e79325c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337760} {:answer/id #uuid "cb765184-ca7f-53c4-8a04-924ee20493f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bma