ield/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374449} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbdaf699-fde6-5e0c-8c57-38703b6634eb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47c92d4d-2e85-56bd-8425-12a1633613d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-181789" :question/problem "![](images/54/54153dcd97ac6471956b6db34f175d1ee622c9bf74e85f93d5e303a7842d24ed.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}<x<{{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}<y<{{field-5}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A point $P(x,y)$ lies inside the rectangle if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2<x<6,\\,2<y<5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2<x<6,\\,\\,2<y<5}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cb50bd4-b4db-58f3-8828-aecfc16414e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374455} {:answer/id #uuid "7f20ed8c-1e38-535a-adee-a5e7a8ca7ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374456} {:answer/id #uuid "eb2c6c4d-f0c1-52b5-8270-8048a445138e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374457} {:answer/id #uuid "173f8bc5-0e7d-5cc4-bf37-7b1f1cf66539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374458} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4bae04-ef6f-51cc-be19-e28e2999