-a768-a274952fa57b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2b44e41-a752-5cb8-969d-6a84dd5dccbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374480} {:answer/id #uuid "d595c980-9da9-5dbe-bc96-5e70733ce625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374481} {:answer/id #uuid "da53ca8e-a69a-52fc-b090-2ce4f140771b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374482} {:answer/id #uuid "bb60e137-34a0-5ef3-abdb-08f2da979d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374483} {:answer/id #uuid "780ff5d8-866a-5aee-924b-e10858d57391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374484}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374482} :answer-field/id #uuid "852ea0e3-2448-5d7b-ab53-0dbf10533be7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c5b2d74-698c-58cf-808c-b4cad536b3ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-181805" :question/problem "![](images/40/40f8e6728cd7108f5026bd87debfbf60b616965686065c8e60f0d3ab741e52e4.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A point $P(x,y)$ lies inside or on the rectangle's edges if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\le x\\le 6,\\,3\\le y\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 6,\\,3\\le y\\le 5}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "296014ff-439c-53ce-b7f8-4e11aadbf4a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374487} {:answer/id #uuid "987ca7ea-6e1c-5921-8dcc-91b3ca2106ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423008}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423008} :answer-field/id #uuid "b79ae90c-0d36-5d1c-8416-c9af790b4f27" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d4de7c3-95e7-59a5-b6dd-15e14af73f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374489}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374489} :answer-field/id #uuid "36599e8f-789f-5518-8d65-81d09037ca61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374488} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77a9cf15-958b-5e1e-b2cb-535037ccdba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374491}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374491} :answer-field/id #uuid "18c16c31-6b5e-5563-acf2-2064877009ae" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1352187-54c7-5a62-9d05-9f2859a738dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-181811" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d13bfa3f5b0a9456c3251e9363c132578ba0d93b1b5a76c5b375c0c1abc7e310.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$64$\n\n$\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=4$ and vertical radius $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=64.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *outside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point outside the region, say, $(5,0).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n4(5)^{2}+16(0)^{2}\\,>\\,64.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}>64.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $4{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=64$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}\\ge 64.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}\\ge 64\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89059596-c90e-5800-b5c8-67b3cfc816fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383635} {:answer/id #uuid "12087dc5-970c-5c09-a6ed-0645ee25d2a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383636} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb1972c-1680-542d-ace5-14a31ee17f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383637} {:answer/id #uuid "bf65f351-c0f8-52d8-8d70-cb8ca2d6955c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383638} {:answer/id #uuid "6396d681-913d-5c4d-908b-51fe8f0f7afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383637} :answer-field/id #uuid "315cd83c-1991-5d33-a3bd-612e91d72c6c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cddd9fc4-2acf-570c-bca2-07ad5c56e09c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383641} {:answer/id #uuid "c156887b-3706-5f49-b9aa-8629e2ed447b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383642} {:answer/id #uuid "6eac4d1d-32a7-5cee-8c24-c1ea679dd25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383643} {:answer/id #uuid "b87352e2-0f30-5478-aa59-2d6a8739b4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383644} {:answer/id #uuid "ab261920-5fe2-5041-9504-48b190edfd5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383641} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7c5b80-cf72-50b6-beaf-a55cb5a4e731" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22bcbd45-a248-5b85-8643-997aed86120a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383647} {:answer/id #uuid "6a012830-1859-5376-b78c-b5ce93fc2b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383648} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ef4af6-694c-5da8-b4a7-045385e71bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383649} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8c9e4b-6ad1-5568-8838-c14f8064fb2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383650} {:answer/id #uuid "318d1154-0e6f-5b9b-9567-fa06e0f161e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383651}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383649} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1c14e5c-4f2d-5c9e-8b56-99780514402e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc6d9b64-fae9-5e89-abfa-9eb8e573a546" :question/math-academy-id "q-181683" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2591e9da960008980cf96184975ef19713735814183a97ca8c8f784536fced5.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x-3\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,x+4\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x-3$ and *below* the line $y=x+4.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x-3,\\,y<x+4.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x-3<y<x+4.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=-x-3$ and $y=x+4$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\n-x-3\\le y\\le x+4\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x-3\\le y\\le x+4\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383659 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74d9ee25-e7b7-58b0-991a-fa581220392e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383661} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b365be-0692-5c0b-8b15-7c5fd1d7d41a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383662} {:answer/id #uuid "42a9b21c-ead6-55af-91ba-c961d71587eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383663} {:answer/id #uuid "a616613f-24e0-5e78-a6af-35b1e85ac687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383664} {:answer/id #uuid "646c8f0b-9b88-5aa3-b837-7926fe6c42a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383665}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383665} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97e82ee-e977-5931-8615-3091934077ec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "159abfe8-35fa-5253-8a0d-de096ebe3643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383667} {:answer/id #uuid "31d011d9-ca80-5fb9-bb5d-2a1be8732dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383668} {:answer/id #uuid "2832b6ca-39f6-5caa-9798-210f0c85108b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383669} {:answer/id #uuid "ac49aba0-bc6e-556c-b74a-47021eb1833c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383670} {:answer/id #uuid "6815f1fd-54d1-578c-bc15-fd34cb371fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383671} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3294a0-2af0-58c3-bbe2-ff85cbc3132a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383672}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383670} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ea587c5-1117-5d17-8452-4a06c1cb4e98" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fe75e6b-cd24-5aa3-ab89-59af0e344d4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-182017" :question/problem "![](images/45/45690fd9ef862b1c8f0a2bb34bba2d305cd3c723ccde09648133b64006ad8f25.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=2.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\ny<2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y<2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901763ea-91a4-5ccc-9fd1-7a5abd771549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387854} {:answer/id #uuid "e471dd7f-cf5c-5449-bdd5-1669c5ee7ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,2⟩=14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387855} {:answer/id #uuid "be245f9d-2743-5776-a695-325f9e3f765e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387856} {:answer/id #uuid "e50391f5-f264-5d75-924b-8343f68bda37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387857} {:answer/id #uuid "9c146846-53c1-5f64-8789-a2b060a469a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,6,2⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387858}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387856} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a27afd-b25c-559e-94cd-93712349e320" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78e0dc1f-5e12-54f0-b00c-492a979933d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127937" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-1,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-4,1,3)$ and $B(2,3,5).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-4,1,3)$ and $B(2,3,5)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,3,5⟩-⟨-4,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨6,2,2⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e8820fb-a6d0-5faf-9981-71cb5d041f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,-3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,0⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387875} {:answer/id #uuid "6c78dd0f-845d-5bcb-9b44-79f85c755d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,9,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨-7,0,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387876} {:answer/id #uuid "d00473ec-47a7-55f6-8a63-b87befe37369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,6,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387877} {:answer/id #uuid "d3744926-06d2-5a5f-a5e2-07abcc77fabc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,1,0⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387878} {:answer/id #uuid "47647d85-f672-5262-8d4f-f0d7a9258831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,-6,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,0,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387879}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387878} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab2fab9-a504-560f-bbc5-2ac638b9790f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a275fd86-a21a-5ef1-ae5c-9df806e069b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128400" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $7x+y-3=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨7,1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+y-3 & =0 \\\\ y & =3-7x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$, we get $y=3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,3,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,3,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,1,0⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bcab70b-517a-5271-894e-c4b561597fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,-2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,5⟩+t⟨3,6,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387889} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4c8236-4299-5664-9863-74ff3a24010c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,2⟩+t⟨4,3,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387890} {:answer/id #uuid "37f487f1-ec69-5071-83c4-95ce287eda90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-7,3⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨3,5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387891} {:answer/id #uuid "46c96bf2-16f7-52a0-a229-e72577f23ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387892} {:answer/id #uuid "03dc462d-3599-5fba-aad0-834967006884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,2⟩+s⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨7,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387893}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387892} :answer-field/id #uuid "99d29468-156d-5427-b6e3-354339252a04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d8e167e-ba7b-5746-8896-10f0f88087c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128501" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(7,-2,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,2,1⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,-5,19⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,4,7⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(7,-2,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨7,-2,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5688ffe4-a344-59de-904d-69d4ee154888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387959} {:answer/id #uuid "f1894930-5724-5ec7-9314-304ee3857bbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨1,-2,-1⟩+t⟨5,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387960} {:answer/id #uuid "36f474e9-d65e-5772-a687-55109749a47b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,-2⟩+t⟨3,5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387961} {:answer/id #uuid "cb27fd48-3d2d-5982-947b-b3e559f28c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,1,2⟩+t⟨-3,1,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387962} {:answer/id #uuid "17405e35-9e5b-5d7e-a665-511b494914e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387963} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b619d06-46ec-54c2-b23b-cc9a1e50c422" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8ae8a52-91d4-5f03-bbaf-4e5a85108c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-128741" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(1,-2,3),\\,Q(3,-4,2),$ and $R(4,3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-4,2⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =⟨4,3,2⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,5,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨1,-2,3⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+s\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+t\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\ r & =⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c5c0f5-cea3-5255-8903-d2285b902635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387966} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5a335a-8c39-5296-9221-80718d983791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387967} {:answer/id #uuid "a1feedd1-adb2-5c03-b2da-3a56801de734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,0⟩+t⟨2,-3,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387968} {:answer/id #uuid "9a555223-84bf-5c63-a527-b176aedbb599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨-1,3,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387969} {:answer/id #uuid "0604c24b-d46b-5997-bc46-46a6a514d076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,-1,1⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387966} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f3ed1e-aca6-5323-9130-d1a84b4303b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0a7f0779-a02e-54b4-a490-a401988e7022" :question/math-academy-id "q-128745" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $D(3,2,-1),\\,E(3,1,-2),$ and $F(5,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨5,1,2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $d=⟨3,2,-1⟩$ of the point $D,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s\\overset{\\to }{DE}+t\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\ r & =⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c59e6db-4da7-5225-a15a-a3a8cb35b39b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,0⟩=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390850} {:answer/id #uuid "bd098e59-549e-5866-8e21-9d7e91238120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩=⟨3,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390851} {:answer/id #uuid "98de472d-01a5-57b0-ae88-2854366aa900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390852} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd5498c-0b9a-5a68-b60e-60a0077ea6de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390853} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0c9d73-79d9-533b-b84a-27c343b14c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,0⟩=⟨-1,2,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390852} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0db56fe-4519-5626-a551-2a57e0daa778" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390849}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8d650e6-dfa8-594c-8c20-f63e265d1d5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-33026" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point  $Q(3,2,0)$ and is  perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨1,-2,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨3,2,0⟩,$ and $n=⟨1,-2,5⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩ & =⟨3,2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩ & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f8e54c-0615-5591-b542-0b782cd89daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391182} {:answer/id #uuid "de1fd91f-8a5e-51f3-8dc2-a58537f9f1b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391183} {:answer/id #uuid "c540887b-e7fe-5d55-972c-cf0a8340ba96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,0,4⟩=⟨-1,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391184} {:answer/id #uuid "796aa680-c468-5852-b522-12b6bd2cf262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩=⟨-3,0,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391185} {:answer/id #uuid "eee5c6a8-ae14-524b-a64c-c15d96be1896" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,0,4⟩=23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391182} :answer-field/id #uuid "54786791-8d86-5133-85dc-e9b4fbb89dbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa8c997f-15c5-5b2a-b1e2-bd26aa6233d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-33324" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,0,4)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-t \\\\ y &=4+3t \\\\ z &=-6+5t.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨-3,0,4⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-t \\\\ y &=4+3t \\\\ z &=-6+5t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨2,4,-6⟩+t\\text{ }\\underbrace{⟨-1,3,5⟩}_{v}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-1,3,5⟩.$ So, a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-1,3,5⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩ & =⟨-3,0,4⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,3,5⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e02ac0-3e89-5c73-aee7-9f2de3148d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} {:answer/id #uuid "8ffc566d-8d4c-53c3-af4b-b2d7a4d35946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391685} {:answer/id #uuid "efc39529-4f0f-5e00-b796-0c632007c03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391686} {:answer/id #uuid "f83846d5-42d7-540e-ad5c-05350b13e9fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391687} {:answer/id #uuid "0693f405-c3d1-5022-a785-4b3d44119374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aebbae6-4b97-5e3f-9a17-15682100023d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b07ac22-3309-5bc0-ac4b-6e1be0e5a45e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33823" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,1,0⟩+t⟨-1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,2,2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨0,2,2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,2,-2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "679c7dcb-5145-5780-81d8-87024bb1bd27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392996} {:answer/id #uuid "b5515e80-84a8-5eb8-a2be-ba588012a168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392997} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d8dd1b-1865-5a25-92a3-6c3b04aadb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392998} {:answer/id #uuid "88367f38-9b3d-5d8d-9f17-294ee6119dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392999} {:answer/id #uuid "e1992dff-615f-5a0d-8cc8-9fbb461f55a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393000}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393000} :answer-field/id #uuid "9228779e-fa16-5c42-9940-9025c4863d96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "559832c2-15b2-5b81-bb2b-4adab3a391f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-70647" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-4,5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $n=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is normal to the plane. \n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d75490e5-1509-58bb-9763-c438183b853c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,0,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393017} {:answer/id #uuid "aeda2ffa-42b4-52c6-88ee-ca624f7cbd32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,0,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393018} {:answer/id #uuid "e668ab95-81b2-5487-a8db-a7ad8d3973d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,1,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393019} {:answer/id #uuid "9538cda3-e06b-5fe5-b129-c566cce61ce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,1,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393020} {:answer/id #uuid "937f4290-2d11-5090-a4a2-afbc778336d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,-2,-4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393020} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca2ac9ba-0e12-54e9-981f-caf50c21ada3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73c1d5d9-6a23-5438-8d9f-6779511254e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-70818" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $2x+y-2z-4=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z-4 & =0 \\\\ -2z & =-2x-y+4 \\\\ z & =x+\\frac{1}{2}y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-2.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-2)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,1,-2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f840eb8f-ab9a-5f24-8c61-1495e09eec29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,-13⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393024} {:answer/id #uuid "91ee1039-c30b-5d26-b83c-09088d137cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393025} {:answer/id #uuid "23c5e4b7-8bec-5100-9926-e941a39c382d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨7,-1,-13⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393026} {:answer/id #uuid "4d0de0e0-0dc6-5fa0-9f0d-4286598f473e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,7,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393027} {:answer/id #uuid "4781d9fd-c985-5f91-b6b3-1be2153657f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393028}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393028} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd843a19-122b-52dc-97b2-1085325976eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7d906b68-2682-5ae7-a3b1-5cdc64fb4dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-70824" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $7y-z-13=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨0,7,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y-z-13 & =0 \\\\ z & =7y-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=-13.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-13)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-13⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,7,-1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4fb71df-948c-5126-86b0-9d79cb4c0fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393031} {:answer/id #uuid "75ed4713-5dc0-5929-8f1a-ae29368dccf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393032} {:answer/id #uuid "14d6c7a2-54c1-5ce2-9906-4d55cf87f498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393033} {:answer/id #uuid "32938842-cdd7-5118-b60e-0c5d24a27836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393034} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4da8ff-198b-50e0-8319-7a9af39b8918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393035}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393032} :answer-field/id #uuid "b14d7746-5f36-5ef0-9936-be22c8877f39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee04e6aa-94ba-5e6d-a904-4a34aac7a757" :question/math-academy-id "q-70827" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨1,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a5ad7cf-e4ff-58ff-83bd-f3f78d2bf29c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393038} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5c0679-e0fe-53ca-b25e-60be64c06d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393039} {:answer/id #uuid "178672b3-37b3-5655-842f-d4da500e1495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393040} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a20d75-694b-5bf5-8c25-578546bfef99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393041} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c1542c-9778-5777-a91d-fc1ba92f6b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393042}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393038} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb32e226-7bfb-5486-b6de-65722871d5f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be607052-6286-5c45-a7b0-2a7d8e65a24b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70892" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,2,1⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393043 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493da2a3-c2b1-5d90-946c-32226dc19e64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,-2⟩=⟨-3,4,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393045} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7fa3af-d391-569e-bc17-106f3e9396bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=⟨3,-5,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393046} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe2b282-7f73-5949-a7f3-cc5ddf1e2530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393047} {:answer/id #uuid "949e581b-c362-5470-828e-687788c962cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,-2⟩=-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393048} {:answer/id #uuid "1521f0fb-a511-5bc0-893e-2c6a06cceff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393049}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393049} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ef96c8-9198-5e30-8832-aa55a71dc6d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca2b2271-1ec0-5a3e-b5ac-687d91668797" :question/math-academy-id "q-70895" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3t \\\\ y &=3+4t \\\\ z &=4-t.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-5,-2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3t \\\\ y &=3+4t \\\\ z &=4-t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨2,3,4⟩+t\\text{ }\\underbrace{⟨-3,4,-1⟩}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840901d2-388a-56b4-b2ed-4aa835792fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393059} {:answer/id #uuid "3a999e63-69bc-5b5b-ba4a-b3d5b35bdaf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} {:answer/id #uuid "a9567360-7eeb-5790-a68a-54789a38c8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393061} {:answer/id #uuid "0abc7499-ef02-5049-b4d5-92446ade1dde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,20⟩+t⟨0,3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393062} {:answer/id #uuid "d56ba868-cc5e-5eb8-8190-756b44636c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,0,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,7⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} :answer-field/id #uuid "74bd7e12-82f3-5b83-88f9-1acb2c12ad74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1e3ae2d-0bf0-5679-8209-36898e366f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70981" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $H(-3,2,7)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨3,-1,20⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-4⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $H(-3,2,7)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $h=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =h+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11fe6c60-77f7-596d-b73e-0a2b1a46b507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨2,-9,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393066} {:answer/id #uuid "18c27f61-10ac-5e9a-9262-ba682e6d266e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393067} {:answer/id #uuid "a673c983-c8f1-5b15-8abb-116913587299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393068} {:answer/id #uuid "f377602b-aa7b-52c3-8d62-a25cd478c050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨0,-6,-1⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393069} {:answer/id #uuid "37a16cbe-c7b9-5d98-99c1-895ad8adbfef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨2,-9,0⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393070}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393068} :answer-field/id #uuid "141932d6-a6f5-58b4-ba12-7fe47a40ab43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "901f1360-df93-5e5e-ac60-c5607de4f628" :question/math-academy-id "q-71036" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(3,6,2),\\,Q(2,-9,0)$, and $R(3,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,-9,0⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-15,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =⟨3,0,1⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨3,6,2⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+s\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+t\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\ r & =⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c55c069-4c02-5970-a366-2d87c0faefc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,4,1⟩+t⟨5,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398349} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c9d880-a1e1-5be5-8507-819f78ea66e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,8,11⟩+s⟨-3,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398350} {:answer/id #uuid "ee62040f-08f9-5abf-8ec9-6681c3d75424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,5,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398351} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9a749a-2d90-567b-9b9e-9eea1e14d989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbcf038-f3dc-5a71-b0c2-b0f15532c018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,11⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} :answer-field/id #uuid "f112cd0f-0678-5784-90d3-7e1ee7077df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fce542a-476c-5ad1-ad5a-b30b8a4bb006" :question/math-academy-id "q-128499" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(1,5,13)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,12,5⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-9,21,2⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,5,-3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7adad79-7530-548f-8ef5-d7d669e56a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473314} {:answer/id #uuid "3e638fd2-f5b6-56e4-a961-6af8957d8b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473315}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473315} :answer-field/id #uuid "a473b682-7626-5413-963d-7ed5605a64f2" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/94/9484c41b7b3141c697d25e72b106f018cb78f2bc68f2d671555c8d347f37f726.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f30a22a7-4bfd-5473-b723-c45d77507594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473316} {:answer/id #uuid "09191b98-cda3-5c87-82cd-aa5bca0c44ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473316} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a18be48-97e8-5987-8dfc-ecda00586f8b" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/e7/e7d5fdbccc6e9fc256924810e9fb7867fb30a52edad837a7dbb55c3fee857901.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66355ab9-c052-5d61-9dd1-e8de20763389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473318} {:answer/id #uuid "f502b7b1-cfd1-55bc-bf4e-4a5fb1dfba9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473319}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473318} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a32fca9-dae5-5c00-9560-d1306e445f41" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/cf/cf2db417b6f90899d1264ecb763f90c3bb654e37be4abc4221e912b2a4dc09ee.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82f2815d-a760-5a7e-b3a4-18ea182996e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74214" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.  \n\n- Diagram I is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. There are vectors  $a=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$  in the subset for which ${a}_{1}>0$ and ${a}_{2}>0.$   But then\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}-{a}_{1} \\\\ -{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is diagram I only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86eb0777-d080-53e8-b004-79a014639bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473088} {:answer/id #uuid "7872a4e4-6631-5d82-b92a-e36225c1be50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473089}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473088} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7455588-72d5-550c-9183-e46e0782f4aa" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/53/5303e5de04148fbd414db26930d50d5c0cd4ef19af5a46afaf4b312966cdfded.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79c0d29f-bfc2-506c-909d-d2ee04efe33c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473090} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1c9619-2805-5f10-9fdb-01a2befb4460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473091}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473090} :answer-field/id #uuid "11293092-de1e-51d5-b24b-3326cc42091a" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/cc/ccdca51aef8ee61c23d3f3a81b1e4673598ffdde88cb4f58b4b35bb76886f524.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9299db-52e0-589b-b002-e37948bbdadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473092} {:answer/id #uuid "474e300d-b0ad-520c-b70a-93c1e5e2e177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473093}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473092} :answer-field/id #uuid "19219c0d-23df-589d-82c4-a37e066f5d0f" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/e4/e495be81f41917740b46b1bfd43fd5cde69041981463c3dbbd96e55d206a8806.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6257fe4e-839a-565a-8b2c-f714a654f8e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669177} {:answer/id #uuid "6345f7b4-6ad0-50c1-bece-b8d368359b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669178}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186669178} :answer-field/id #uuid "57d88627-fcc0-5ab9-8ab9-960f9a4986ee" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "befb255b-f1bd-5c00-bc58-981c00e76ebb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35574" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace.  In this case we also have that the vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9099832-9536-5764-b8f9-82d9f50c96e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409896}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409896} :answer-field/id #uuid "1979d639-7c7b-51e8-9e83-40721047de2a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409897} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53607ff6-5913-50ea-923c-e269930ccd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409894}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409894} :answer-field/id #uuid "38cdacac-1881-5ec8-b9e9-d206d7013904" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d74e258e-f0dd-579c-9148-3c83bfa32b0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409895}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409895} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1c0edf-ff99-50f4-9ecf-942f2ee605d1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6164b43d-cb18-5fe7-a896-e7c6ff8846af" :question/math-academy-id "q-181810" :question/problem "![](images/59/592dc9d0d4713406cf9bf9c6ad966cb4446420113aa0e94fcfdcdb35b6471a9c.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$144$\n\n$\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=3$ and vertical radius $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n16{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=144.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *inside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point inside the region, say, $(0,0).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n16(0)^{2}+9(0)^{2}\\,<\\,144.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n16{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}<144.\n$$\n\nNotice that we use $<$ since the boundary is excluded from the set (the boundary curve is dashed).\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,16{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}<144\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "218576bd-e46c-5334-968e-a8f88468df74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410865} {:answer/id #uuid "43be24cf-8641-5f97-b8d8-732e9a3edde2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{11} \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410869} {:answer/id #uuid "75d57370-81cc-5500-be9a-c76059ef4dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410879} {:answer/id #uuid "a70d42f7-d1f2-52ef-9c49-8609198f6893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410886} {:answer/id #uuid "f24ae82e-856b-58e1-b7dd-3cd42518a542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410891}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410879} :answer-field/id #uuid "9736daed-5120-541b-9af8-2423772b6d03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1c09c350-e142-585c-9d61-fa93c5184487" :question/math-academy-id "q-128469" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $M(-4,3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$  and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $M$ is $p=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$  and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3315c99a-bf65-5d24-a5cd-d108af0b9169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,3,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410868} {:answer/id #uuid "49c23de5-10ac-588e-b906-2f601c3ee4cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410870} {:answer/id #uuid "58daaedf-85bc-5389-a9f1-135d9cf2dc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,6,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410872} {:answer/id #uuid "68dd536e-0595-5b7f-bbf4-086bbda96dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,6,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410875} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d316ee-8c43-5cbe-ae4e-5f0454d179ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410870} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d97d655-a539-5ca4-b364-2c12300cff27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4fcca2b7-695c-58b7-b034-c1fa748f47da" :question/math-academy-id "q-128496" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,-5,1⟩+s⟨3,-6,0⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨2,-5,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-6,0⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =6i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨6,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨6,3,3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f06646-216c-5c67-9be6-f9c0e54523f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-3,-2,0⟩+t⟨1,0,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410867} {:answer/id #uuid "56c396c7-54c7-56b3-83a2-5e6b3f8f1725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨4,2,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410871} {:answer/id #uuid "8e59d870-815b-50b7-be77-2034640ef7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410882} {:answer/id #uuid "918bb145-9b81-5373-9e09-80bc4d524835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨-3,-2,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410883} {:answer/id #uuid "c9066316-4e88-5b51-afd6-db0ca189a8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,0,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410890}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410871} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffaa26fc-cae0-5499-800c-9dd489ee2f5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59e1275b-72d1-5efa-8072-c2d963838f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71049" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(-3,-2,0)$ and $V(1,0,-1)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨1,0,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨-3,-2,0⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨4,2,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ac6b7cf-9cdf-544b-857c-d76a43c0147d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410864} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd93671-feef-59db-be6f-a0f31a8f3e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410873} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7d541c-0806-5629-b333-ae0ae03e2711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410874} {:answer/id #uuid "a96f0586-bad6-55c1-a8e8-5a58ec0473a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410887} {:answer/id #uuid "bf93f0ea-48e2-58b4-984d-09176408a3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410889}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410874} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d611d3d-5569-5f15-bdad-b3556e59c440" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e3aacfb-29e6-50e7-83f4-efffd6632659" :question/math-academy-id "q-70967" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $R(\\sqrt{2},3,-1)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$  and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $R$ is $p=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$  and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1.5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}]}
